import RequestProject.Wikidata.Core

/-!
# Redundant subclass edges and their removal

A `P279` statement is *redundant* when its endpoints remain connected after the
statement is deleted.  The main results say that deleting a redundant statement
preserves the derived subclass and instance relations exactly.

This is the formal content behind the review-only repair operation
`removeRedundantSuperclass` in `RequestProject.Epistemic.Repair`: a redundant
edge is provably removable *without changing what the ontology says*, which is a
strictly weaker (and different) claim than saying the superclass is wrong.
-/

